                        <field name="dc_date">beginning and end of the 9th century </field>
                        <field name="dc_description">This composit manuscript consists of two parts. It contains copies of two works by the Church Father Jerome († 420), the Quaestiones hebraicae in Genesim (addressing questions about the translation of the first book of Exodus from the Hebrew) and De situ et nominibus locorum hebraicorum (about Biblical place names), together with an anonymous commentary on the Old Testament Songs of Salomon and the Instituta regularia divinae legis by Junilius Africanus (ca. 551). The first part was produced at the beginning of the 9th century, the second at the end of the 9th century. The codex retains its orginal Carolingian binding. </field>
